        "original_id": "b1d2adef-ca9e-53ac-b5b7-0f1616f0ab94",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Richard Curtis, Domhnall Gleeson, Rachel McAdams, Bill Nighy, Vanessa Kirby, Peter Morgan\n- Films and TV series: About Time, Great Expectations, The Crown\n- Organizations: BBC, Netflix, Dublin Institute of Technology, British Academy Television Awards\n- Concepts: time travel\n\nFacts:\n- Vanessa Kirby starred as Estella in the BBC adaptation of Great Expectations in 2011.\n- About Time is a 2013 British romantic comedy-drama film about a young man who can time travel and tries to change his past to improve his future.\n- Richard Curtis wrote and directed About Time in 2013.\n- About Time stars Domhnall Gleeson, Rachel McAdams, and Bill Nighy.\n- Vanessa Kirby starred as Joanna in Richard Curtis's romantic comedy About Time in 2013.\n- Domhnall Gleeson, born on 12 May 1983, is an Irish actor and writer.\n- Domhnall Gleeson received a Bachelor of Arts in Media Arts from Dublin Institute of Technology.\n- Vanessa Kirby portrays Princess Margaret in Peter Morgan's Netflix series The Crown and was nominated for the British Academy Television Award for Best Supporting Actress for that role.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
